WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:05.890 --> 00:00:38.350
[Dramatic music]

00:00:48.280 --> 00:00:51.020
[Narrator:] Let's face it.

00:00:51.160 --> 00:00:56.280
The threat of hydrogen bomb warfare is the
greatest danger our nation has ever known.

00:00:56.289 --> 00:01:00.420
Enemy jet bombers carrying nuclear weapons
can sweep over a variety of routes

00:01:00.420 --> 00:01:06.090
and drop bombs on any important target in
the United States.

00:01:06.090 --> 00:01:10.920
The threat of this destruction has affected
our way of life in every city, town, and village

00:01:10.920 --> 00:01:12.350
from coast to coast.

00:01:12.350 --> 00:01:15.420
These are the signs of the times.

00:01:15.420 --> 00:01:20.079
[Air raid sirens sound]

00:01:20.079 --> 00:01:24.399
Only in practice now, a rehearsal, a training
exercise,

00:01:24.399 --> 00:01:29.090
but tomorrow this siren may mean the real
thing.

00:01:29.090 --> 00:01:31.710
And if you hear it as you drive in your auto,

00:01:31.710 --> 00:01:35.950
as you sit in your office, or work at your
bank,

00:01:35.950 --> 00:01:40.320
wherever you are, what will you do?

00:01:40.320 --> 00:01:42.960
What will happen to you?

00:01:42.960 --> 00:01:49.299
Let's face it. Your life, the fate of your
community, and the fate of your nation

00:01:49.299 --> 00:01:54.229
depends on what you do when enemy bombers
head for our cities,

00:01:54.229 --> 00:01:58.130
and that is why civil defense was organized.

00:01:58.130 --> 00:02:03.030
To teach you how to survive in the thermonuclear
age by taking shelter

00:02:03.030 --> 00:02:08.390
or by evacuating your area as directed.

00:02:08.390 --> 00:02:13.420
Civil defense will teach you how to take care
of yourself, your family, and neighbors,

00:02:13.420 --> 00:02:17.600
how to get official instructions and act according
to plan.

00:02:18.480 --> 00:02:22.180
In time of atomic attack, the usual professional
services,

00:02:22.180 --> 00:02:24.680
police, fire, welfare, hospital, and ambulance

00:02:24.680 --> 00:02:31.050
could be bombed out, too busy, or unable to
get to you and your family.

00:02:31.050 --> 00:02:35.230
Civil defense control points would function
as the nerve centers

00:02:35.230 --> 00:02:41.480
for dispatch of organized assistants to disaster
areas from outside the target districts.

00:02:41.480 --> 00:02:45.920
Every preparation is being made to deal with
emergency conditions which would be created

00:02:45.920 --> 00:02:48.470
by enemy attack.

00:02:48.470 --> 00:02:52.769
To provide for communication with the public
during an actual attack,

00:02:52.769 --> 00:02:57.420
our broadcasting industry and the federal
government developed Conelrad.

00:02:57.420 --> 00:03:02.019
This system permits the broadcasting of official
news and civil defense instructions

00:03:02.019 --> 00:03:07.379
without helping enemy navigators find our
cities by following radial beams.

00:03:07.379 --> 00:03:13.680
The Conelrad frequencies are 640 and 1240
on your standard radio dial.

00:03:13.680 --> 00:03:17.879
A hazard unique to nuclear warfare is radioactive fallout.

00:03:17.879 --> 00:03:24.879
Unseen, unheard, and odorless, this substance can only be detected with sensitive instruments.

00:03:25.799 --> 00:03:29.860
Special training is necessary for radiological
safety experts.

00:03:29.860 --> 00:03:35.090
Their duties will be to check radiation levels
in both damaged areas and probable fallout areas.

00:03:36.830 --> 00:03:39.909
When sufficient warning time can be obtained by early detection

00:03:39.909 --> 00:03:44.269
of approaching enemy aircraft, withdrawal
from key target cities

00:03:44.269 --> 00:03:49.439
or fallout areas may be ordered by local civil
defense authority.

00:03:49.439 --> 00:03:53.450
The instinct of survival is inherent in all
of us

00:03:53.450 --> 00:03:59.959
and national survival requires that each one
of us assume his share of the responsibility.

00:03:59.959 --> 00:04:03.909
There is work to be done and each must cooperate.

00:04:03.909 --> 00:04:08.459
Opportunities for training with the Red Cross
and other groups are everywhere.

00:04:08.459 --> 00:04:14.409
The combined efforts of many trained individuals are needed to make civil defense a forceful reality.

00:04:15.980 --> 00:04:19.579
This training is invaluable in preparation
for enemy attack

00:04:19.579 --> 00:04:25.260
or the savage fury of nature.

00:04:25.260 --> 00:04:30.470
Experience in past disasters has proved the
value of advanced training and the need

00:04:30.470 --> 00:04:35.640
for more stockpiling of emergency food supplies,
medicines, and other critical items

00:04:35.640 --> 00:04:38.180
to care for the injured and the homeless.

00:04:38.180 --> 00:04:41.030
However, it was the awesome power of atomic
energy

00:04:41.030 --> 00:04:45.420
as demonstrated in wartime use that brought
to sharp focus the new problems

00:04:45.420 --> 00:04:50.290
concerning human survival and the urgent need
for a civil defense program

00:04:50.290 --> 00:04:54.170
based on facts about the atomic bomb.

00:04:54.170 --> 00:04:57.790
Opportunities to gain this information came
with the study of structures

00:04:57.790 --> 00:05:03.390
in controlled atomic tests conducted at Eniwetok
Atoll in the central Pacific.

00:05:03.390 --> 00:05:08.900
The main objective of testing is weapons development
to strengthen national security,

00:05:08.900 --> 00:05:14.130
but also included are scientific experiments
for the Atomic Energy Commission,

00:05:14.130 --> 00:05:17.940
military projects for the air force, army,
and navy,

00:05:17.940 --> 00:05:21.550
and defense tests for the Federal Civil Defense
Administration

00:05:21.550 --> 00:05:28.550
primarily concerned with the effects of nuclear
weapons on cities, industries, and people.

00:05:28.780 --> 00:05:33.320
The tremendous effects of heat and blast on
modern structures raise important questions

00:05:33.320 --> 00:05:36.370
concerning their durability and safety.

00:05:36.370 --> 00:05:39.940
Likewise the amount of damage done to our
industrial potential

00:05:39.940 --> 00:05:45.310
will have a serious effect upon our ability
to recover from an atomic attack.

00:05:45.310 --> 00:05:48.690
Transportation facilities are vital to a modern
city.

00:05:48.690 --> 00:05:53.410
The nation's lifeblood could be cut if its
traffic arteries were severed.

00:05:53.410 --> 00:05:58.380
These questions are of great interest not
only to citizens in metropolitan centers,

00:05:58.380 --> 00:06:02.250
but also to those in rural areas who may be
in a danger zone

00:06:02.250 --> 00:06:07.220
because of radioactive fallout from today's
larger weapons.

00:06:07.220 --> 00:06:11.370
We could get many of the answers to these questions by constructing a complete city

00:06:11.370 --> 00:06:13.790
at our Nevada proving ground

00:06:13.790 --> 00:06:20.790
and then exploding a nuclear bomb over it.

00:06:21.200 --> 00:06:26.580
We could study the effects of damage over
a wide area under all conditions,

00:06:26.580 --> 00:06:28.590
and plan civil defense measures accordingly.

00:06:28.590 --> 00:06:32.860
But such a gigantic undertaking is not feasible.

00:06:32.860 --> 00:06:39.860
Instead we build representative units of a
test city with steel and stone and brick and mortar,

00:06:40.620 --> 00:06:45.260
with precision and skill as though it were
to last a thousand years, but

00:06:45.260 --> 00:06:51.250
but it's a weird, fantastic city, a creation right out of science fiction.

00:06:51.250 --> 00:06:55.150
A city like no other on the face of the earth.

00:06:55.150 --> 00:07:00.330
Homes neat and clean and completely furnished
that will never be occupied;

00:07:00.330 --> 00:07:04.760
bridges, massive girders of steel spanning
the empty desert.

00:07:04.760 --> 00:07:10.150
Railway tracks that lead to nowhere, for this
is the end of the line.

00:07:10.150 --> 00:07:15.650
But every element in these tests is carefully planned as to its design and location in the area.

00:07:16.430 --> 00:07:22.530
a variety of materials and building techniques are often represented in a single structure.

00:07:22.530 --> 00:07:26.460
Every brick, beam, and board will have its
story to tell.

00:07:26.460 --> 00:07:29.430
When pieced together these will give some
of the answers

00:07:29.430 --> 00:07:34.820
and some of the information we need to survive
in the nuclear age.

00:07:34.820 --> 00:07:40.180
At varying distances from ground zero, the
point of detonation, numerous experimental

00:07:40.180 --> 00:07:42.660
elements are assembled.

00:07:42.660 --> 00:07:48.240
Underground structures and facilities of various
types play their part in duplicating the complexity

00:07:48.240 --> 00:07:50.160
of the modern city.

00:07:50.160 --> 00:07:54.940
The vast research program includes testing
such items as covering materials,

00:07:54.940 --> 00:08:01.650
paints, varnishes, plastics, also various
fabrics and samples of clothing.

00:08:01.650 --> 00:08:05.520
On the outskirts of our test city, a synthetic forest has been erected

00:08:05.520 --> 00:08:09.320
to determine the protective value of foliage
and trees.

00:08:09.320 --> 00:08:14.190
To give us a ringside view of the event, high-speed
cameras

00:08:14.190 --> 00:08:21.190
stand like lonely sentinels ready to photograph the hurricane of fury.

00:08:22.520 --> 00:08:24.870
Before leaving the test area, a final check
is made

00:08:24.870 --> 00:08:29.870
on the multitude of instruments and technical
devices which will record a variety of blast

00:08:29.870 --> 00:08:32.140
phenomena for future study.

00:08:32.140 --> 00:08:36.659
Now, with all the elements in place, our test city is complete.

00:08:36.659 --> 00:08:43.659
From the air its center will appear as a bullseye to the bombardier at H hour.

00:08:44.220 --> 00:08:47.350
On the morning of shot day official observers,
technicians,

00:08:47.350 --> 00:08:52.040
and scientists gather at News Knob to await
the momentous event.

00:08:52.040 --> 00:08:55.450
This is the pay-off for months of planning
and preparation

00:08:55.450 --> 00:09:01.410
on the part of the Atomic Energy Commission, the military services, civil defense and other test agencies.

00:09:03.160 --> 00:09:07.460
As part of an experiment to observe the phenomenon of atomic

00:09:07.460 --> 00:09:11.690
detonation at close hand, military personnel and defense officials

00:09:11.690 --> 00:09:15.430
dig in within a few miles of ground zero.

00:09:15.430 --> 00:09:20.080
After a final briefing from the officer in
charge just before H hour,

00:09:20.080 --> 00:09:23.130
the men disappear into their foxholes.

00:09:23.130 --> 00:09:25.610
Every precaution has been taken for their
safety.

00:09:25.610 --> 00:09:30.840
They are told to crouch low, shield their
eyes, 

00:09:30.840 --> 00:09:33.430
and remain down until the signal to rise is given.

00:09:33.430 --> 00:09:40.430
Now the moment of greatest anxiety, waiting those last few seconds.

00:09:40.430 --> 00:09:47.250
[Music]

00:09:47.480 --> 00:10:07.760
[Images of buildings collapsing, fires igniting, explosions, bridges crumbling, and trees bending...]

00:10:15.780 --> 00:10:18.760
[Narrator:] Seconds later the blast wave reaches the trenches.

00:10:19.020 --> 00:10:27.220
[Explosive sound]

00:10:27.280 --> 00:10:31.420
[Narrator:] As the tower of smoke and flames looms overhead, one thought is uppermost in all minds:

00:10:31.560 --> 00:10:33.960
Now it's over.

00:10:33.960 --> 00:10:38.340
The fury of it had stunned some, but not one
was injured.

00:10:38.340 --> 00:10:42.640
High above, the smoke ring puffed by atomic
breath rises skyward,

00:10:42.760 --> 00:10:45.340
watched by the men who had faced it.

00:10:45.760 --> 00:10:50.760
A scouting party takes the first look at the
scattered wreckage of the test city.

00:10:50.770 --> 00:10:55.240
The imprint left by the hurricane of fire
and blast remains here for us to read and analyze.

00:10:57.100 --> 00:11:00.200
From studies of ruins and damage such as this,

00:11:00.200 --> 00:11:05.230
we get the hard-to-come-by knowledge that
helps us form rules for survival in modern warfare.

00:11:06.810 --> 00:11:09.460
While only atomic bombs are tested in Nevada,

00:11:09.460 --> 00:11:14.490
the results can be scaled for the larger,
far more powerful thermonuclear weapons.

00:11:14.490 --> 00:11:19.800
A hydrogen bomb will destroy a greater area
than the atomic bomb

00:11:19.800 --> 00:11:24.250
and will release more dangerous radioactive
materials,

00:11:24.250 --> 00:11:29.500
but the problems of rescue caused by blasts and fire along the periphery of damage remain the same.

00:11:30.870 --> 00:11:35.400
In these fringe areas, civil defense training
can save many lives,

00:11:35.400 --> 00:11:40.080
lessen damage from secondary fires, and help
establish emergency facilities.

00:11:41.300 --> 00:11:45.980
Now in a helicopter, the radiological safety
men measure the amount of radiation.

00:11:45.990 --> 00:11:52.620
When readings indicate safety for human beings,
the troops are led in for a tour of the area.

00:11:52.620 --> 00:11:56.380
By doublechecking with Geiger counters every
inch of the route,

00:11:56.380 --> 00:12:02.550
men can now enter safely and confidently areas
spotted with radiological contamination,

00:12:02.550 --> 00:12:07.680
an indication of the progress made in understanding
atomic hazards.

00:12:07.680 --> 00:12:12.640
And thus each test adds to our growing fund of knowledge.

00:12:12.640 --> 00:12:16.420
For it is only by investigating and experimenting
that we get the facts

00:12:16.420 --> 00:12:22.360
to keep our military and civil defense program
up-to-date and effective.

00:12:22.360 --> 00:12:25.800
Every bit of twisted steel makes its contribution.

00:12:25.800 --> 00:12:29.830
Blackened ruins and ashes of a structure add
another chapter.

00:12:29.830 --> 00:12:34.590
The shattered wreckage of a dwelling offers
an eloquent testimonial.

00:12:34.590 --> 00:12:37.360
Piece by piece, like the parts of a jigsaw
puzzle,

00:12:37.360 --> 00:12:40.910
our story is assembled, analyzed, and evaluated.

00:12:41.840 --> 00:12:47.900
Then the survival facts are made available
to you through your local civil defense program.

00:12:48.960 --> 00:12:55.430
In the thermonuclear age, civil defense, like
military defense, must be flexible.

00:12:55.430 --> 00:13:02.430
It must develop and grow even as the forces
that threaten our existence.

00:13:02.690 --> 00:13:07.930
And so until men of goodwill have turned this
awesome power to peaceful uses,

00:13:07.930 --> 00:13:14.930
let us recognize the threat to our way of
life, the threat to our survival,

00:13:15.060 --> 00:13:17.700
and, let's face it.

00:13:17.800 --> 00:13:28.640
[Dramatic music]

